@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# EVA room bridge (proposed, not deployed)
+
+Baseline: Shado `e9dca6c`. This additive API uses existing media storage, quote pricing and durable generation tasks. It does not create reconstruction geometry: its result is generated video with the existing generation receipt.
+
+Configure a dedicated random `SHADO_EVA_BRIDGE_SECRET` of at least 32 bytes on Shado. Keep it server-only; do not reuse Clerk, worker, cron or provider keys. Missing configuration fails closed. No provider keys are shared with EVA.
+
+Set `SHADO_EVA_ALLOWED_ORIGIN` to the exact EVA browser origin, for example `http://127.0.0.1:5173`. HTTPS origins and HTTP loopback origins are accepted; wildcards, credentials, paths and query strings are rejected.
+
+## Automatic authorization handoff
+
+EVA opens `/eva-room-authorize` in a popup while retaining its Window reference. This public sign-in surface embeds Clerk and returns to itself after sign-in. No private data is returned without authenticated API calls.
+
+The popup sends `{type:"eva-room-ready"}` to the configured EVA origin. The opener verifies the event's source is its popup and its origin is the configured Shado HTTPS origin, then responds with:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "eva-room-request",
+  "nonce": "<fresh 32-128 lowercase hex>",
+  "jobId": "<existing EVA UUID>",
+  "taskId": "<durably saved stable Shado UUID>",
+  "assets": [{"id":"photo-1","sha256":"<64 lowercase hex>","size":12345,"mimeType":"image/jpeg"}]
+}
+```
+
+The assets array must contain 5–7 distinct JPEG, PNG or WebP photos. Only descriptors cross this handshake; originals upload after the user starts the authorized attempt in EVA. The popup accepts exactly one valid request, only from its opener and the explicitly configured EVA origin.
+
+The same-origin `proposal` operation constructs a real Shado project through `createEmptyProject`, `applyCommand`, `createGenerationNode` and `prepareGeneration`. It binds each original's source ID and version to its supplied `id`. The fixed recipe is Seedance 2.5 reference-to-video, five seconds, 720p, 16:9 and no audio, with an explicit single-room prompt. It obtains a server quote without calling a provider. The user sees the recipe, current quote and account, chooses a finite cap, and checks explicit approval.
+
+The popup then issues the bounded grant and sends `{type:"eva-room-grant",nonce,jobId,grant}` to the exact opener origin. `grant` contains `token`, `expiresAt`, `taskId`, the frozen serialized `project`, `nodeId`, `recipeHash`, `maximumMicros` and upload `assets` descriptors. EVA must check source, origin, nonce, job ID, stable task ID and every original checksum/size/MIME before storing the bundle privately through its authenticated broker. Never place the token in a URL or browser persistence. The popup does not call submit; the user returns to EVA and chooses Continue.
+
+This handoff requires opener continuity. If a browser/provider security policy severs `window.opener`, it fails visibly rather than falling back to wildcard messaging. Actual popup sign-in/browser behavior and live grants require deployment validation. The page is not a claim of live operational readiness.
+
+`GET /api/eva-room-bridge` reports version, configuration and operations. `POST` accepts JSON, never arbitrary URLs. Grant issuance requires an authenticated **same-origin Shado Clerk session**. Every bearer request independently revalidates that grant's original session, account, organization membership and current terms through existing Shado code. Client owner, payer and role fields are rejected.
+
+## Exact contract
+
+1. Construct one valid serialized Shado Project with one intended image-to-video generation node and JPEG, PNG or WebP references. Use the same exact serialized string for all calls. The node must pass `prepareGeneration` and `parseRecipe`. Images are limited to 12 originals and 20 MiB each.
+2. From the authenticated Shado origin, submit:
+
+```json
+{
+  "operation": "grant",
+  "taskId": "eva-stable-task-id",
+  "project": "<serialized Project>",
+  "nodeId": "generation-node-id",
+  "maximumMicros": 1000000,
+  "assets": [{
+    "sourceId": "photo-source-id",
+    "version": "photo-version-id",
+    "sha256": "<64 lowercase hex>",
+    "size": 12345,
+    "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
+  }],
+  "approved": true
+}
+```
+
+This is explicit approval of **one immutable recipe, one task and an up-to spending cap**, not an unbounded API key. The server signs the verified identity, exact project/recipe hashes, checksummed originals and cap. It returns `{ok,token,expiresAt,taskId,recipeHash,maximumMicros}`. Maximum cap is 100,000,000 USD micros ($100); deployments may impose a lower product limit before issuing. The bearer expires after 15 minutes.
+
+All remaining calls send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
+
+- Upload: `{operation:"media",assetIndex:0,request:{operation:"prepare"}}` returns existing media preparation response. Subsequent requests use the same asset index and existing `{operation:"chunk",assetId,index,base64}` or `{operation:"seal",assetId}` shape. The server resolves the immutable descriptor before accepting an asset ID. Chunk size is 512 KiB. Descriptor hashes are verified when sealing.
+- Quote: `{operation:"quote",project,nodeId}` returns `{ok,quote}` with public frozen quote ID/hash/price/expiry. Quote creation uses existing server pricing. A cap violation is rejected.
+- Submit: `{operation:"submit",project,nodeId,quoteId,recipeHash,maximumMicros}` uses the **exact quote price**, not the delegation ceiling. It returns HTTP 202 `{ok,task}` after durable admission. Existing task validation binds price, account, recipe and input revisions. Count is always one. The grant's task ID is persisted before submission; retry/recovery must never invent a replacement ID.
+- Status: `{operation:"status"}` returns `{ok,task}` or `{ok,task:null}`. A null result means no durable task was found; it is not evidence that an arbitrary previous invocation was never charged.
+- Stop: `{operation:"stop"}` fences the existing task through Shado's cancellation path; an already admitted provider job can still settle.
+- Output descriptor: `{operation:"output",assetId,index:null}`. Output chunk: `{operation:"output",assetId,index:0}`. Only IDs in this exact task's bound completion receipt are allowed. Existing checksum/chunk metadata supports verifying downloaded bytes.
+
+Do not put tokens in URLs, logs, Pages, commits or browser local storage. A local EVA broker should retain one token in private job storage and never expose it in frontend bundles. The authorization page handles authenticated issuance and opener delivery; the EVA broker remains responsible for validating and privately storing the received bundle.
+
+## Recovery and limitations
+
+Task idempotency is durable in the existing Shado task store. Grant authentication is signed and stateless. There is no independent per-grant revocation database: revoke its Clerk session or rotate the dedicated signing key to invalidate grants immediately. Expired grants cannot submit, read or cancel. Reissuing from an authenticated session must preserve the same task and recipe for recovery; it does not create another run. Accepted task execution uses Shado's existing durable manifest and stop semantics after handoff.
+
+The grant is a compact signed payload, not encrypted; treat the complete bearer as confidential. It contains identifiers and checksums, not original media bytes. The API does not authorize a quoted run merely by returning a quote: submission is constrained by the explicit cap approval made at issuance. A product requiring approval after seeing the exact price must withhold submit until that approval and should implement a second signed quote-specific approval step.
+
+Tests: `node --test src/server/eva-room-grant.test.mjs`. These exercise cryptographic tampering, identity-field rejection, lifetime, recipe/project/node binding, media bounds and spending bounds. They are not live Clerk, database, media, provider or end-to-end tests. Run full Shado typecheck and route integration tests in an installed checkout before deployment. No paid call, upload or deployment is required to inspect this patch.
+
+Additional checks: `node --test src/lib/eva-room-handoff.test.mjs` tests exact origins and bounded request packets. `src/server/eva-room-proposal.test.ts` runs the real project constructors/parser/preparer to verify frozen reference order, settings, recipe hash and deterministic task recovery. Browser rendering, keyboard interaction and live Clerk popup redirects remain unverified until the Shado dependencies are available.
